    "text": "To determine how many marbles Cleo had on the third day, we need to follow the steps of the problem carefully.\n\n1. **Initial number of marbles**: Cleo and Ignacio placed 30 marbles in the jar on Monday.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Initial marbles} = 30\n   \\]\n\n2. **Marbles taken the next day**: They took \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\) of the marbles from the jar the next day and divided them equally.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Marbles taken} = \\frac{3}{5} \\times 30 = 18\n   \\]\n   Since they divided the 18 marbles equally, each of them took:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Marbles each} = \\frac{18}{2} = 9\n   \\]\n   So, after the next day, the number of marbles left in the jar is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Marbles left} = 30 - 18 = 12\n   \\]\n\n3. **Marbles taken by Cleo on the third day**: On the third day, Cleo took \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) of the remaining marbles in the jar.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Marbles taken by Cleo} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6\n   \\]\n   So, the number of marbles Cleo had on the third day is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{6}\n   \\]",
